    "independentBasis": "Exercise 678 states y=10^x on the closed interval [-1.2,1.2], step 0.1 and equal 1cm units. The sample count is (1.2-(-1.2))/0.1+1=25. The spec's 640px/12.8-unit horizontal extent and 960px/19.2-unit vertical extent both give 50px/unit; the tall, narrow appearance is therefore correct, not unequal axis scaling. The declared sample coordinates include (-1,0.1), (0,1), (1,10), the lower endpoint (-1.2,0.06309573444801933) and upper endpoint (1.2,15.848931924611133). These agree with the stated exponential, are positive and strictly increasing; a maximum just below 16 is expected.",
    "actualImageObservation": "The complete repaired image shows one increasing, upward-convex curve confined between two solid domain endpoints. It crosses the y axis at 1, has the x=1 marker at y=10, and ends near y=15.85 below the 16 tick without clipping. The negative endpoint and compressed negative samples sit above the x axis, not on/below it; their close spacing follows from the required equal units. Positive arrowheads, x landmarks -1/0/1 and regularly spaced y integer ticks 1-16 are present in one shared frame. The curve has no extension beyond its endpoints and no false second curve. Individual marker count/analytic interpolation error is corroborated by the bound spec and existing authored executable evidence, not claimed to be measured from this single PNG.",
